Project overview
- This is a Chrome extension named LinkedIn Scraper.
- It helps extract LinkedIn Recruiter profile data and copy it to the clipboard as an HTML table.
- The extension has two content-script modes:
  - One for recruiter search results pages.
  - One for a single recruiter profile page.

Main files and roles
- manifest.json
  - Declares the extension metadata and permissions.
  - Registers content scripts for:
    - https://www.linkedin.com/recruiter/smartsearch*
    - https://www.linkedin.com/recruiter/profile/*
  - Loads background.js and jQuery in the background context.
  - Uses a browser action popup via popup.html.

- popup.js
  - Handles the popup button click.
  - Sends a message to the active tab with the command "extract".
  - This triggers the scraping process in the relevant content script.

- background.js
  - Receives scraped HTML from the content script.
  - Copies the HTML to the user clipboard in a formatted way.
  - Uses chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener to listen for messages.

- linkedin_list.js
  - Used when the user is on a LinkedIn Recruiter search results page.
  - Scrapes multiple profiles from the result list.
  - Builds a table of extracted profile information.
  - Sends the final HTML table back to background.js for copying.

- linkedin_profile.js
  - Used when the user is on a single LinkedIn Recruiter profile page.
  - Scrapes one profile and prepares it for clipboard export.
  - Handles profile unlock prompts when needed.

Function-by-function explanation
1) background.js
- copyFormatted(html)
  - Purpose: creates a temporary DOM container, inserts the provided HTML, selects it, and copies it to the clipboard.
  - How it is used: called when the content script sends scraped HTML to the background script.
  - Why it exists: LinkedIn data is copied as rich HTML instead of plain text.

- chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(function(message) {...})
  - Purpose: listens for messages from content scripts.
  - How it is used: receives the scraped HTML object and passes it to copyFormatted(message.html).

2) popup.js
- submit.onclick = function(element) {...}
  - Purpose: runs when the popup button is clicked.
  - How it is used: calls chrome.tabs.query to find the active tab and sends the extract command to the tab.
  - Why it exists: it connects the popup UI to the scraping logic in the page.

3) linkedin_list.js
- generateTable(html_to_insert)
  - Purpose: wraps the extracted rows inside an HTML table and basic styling.
  - How it is used: creates the final HTML document that will be copied to the clipboard.

- generateTableEntry(first, last, role, location, link)
  - Purpose: builds one table row for a single profile.
  - How it is used: called once for each scraped profile while building the final table.

- generateBanner()
  - Purpose: creates or updates a small status banner at the top of the LinkedIn page.
  - How it is used: shows progress messages such as scraping status and completion.

- generateFrame(url)
  - Purpose: creates an invisible iframe pointing to the profile URL.
  - How it is used: allows the script to load a profile page in the background and inspect its contents.

- urlError(frame)
  - Purpose: checks whether the iframe loaded an error page.
  - How it is used: prevents scraping from continuing when LinkedIn returns an unexpected error page.

- lockedProfile(frame)
  - Purpose: waits until the profile page has loaded enough to determine whether the profile is locked.
  - How it is used: used by getProfile() before extracting details.
  - Logic: looks for the presence of the "Recruiting Activity" section and the "Unlock full profile" button.

- unlock(frame)
  - Purpose: attempts to unlock a locked profile by clicking the unlock button if needed.
  - How it is used: called when getProfile() detects a locked profile.

- titleCase(str)
  - Purpose: capitalizes the first letter of each word in a string.
  - How it is used: formats names and location values into a cleaner display format.

- formatName(name)
  - Purpose: splits a full name into first and last names and formats both parts.
  - How it is used: converts raw LinkedIn display names into a usable first/last pair.

- getDetails(frame)
  - Purpose: extracts the profile data from the loaded iframe page.
  - How it is used: called after the profile is confirmed to be unlocked.
  - Extracts:
    - first name
    - last name
    - job title
    - location
    - public profile URL
  - Also tries to improve job title by matching the target company from the search page with the profile experience section.

- getProfile(url)
  - Purpose: wraps the entire profile loading and extraction flow into one asynchronous function.
  - How it is used: called once per profile during run().
  - Workflow:
    - creates an iframe
    - checks if profile is locked
    - unlocks it if necessary
    - extracts details
    - removes the frame

- run()
  - Purpose: main scraping workflow for recruiter search results.
  - How it is used: called when the content script receives the extract command.
  - Workflow:
    - finds all visible profiles on the search page
    - loops through each profile
    - skips profiles marked as not linked
    - loads each profile via getProfile(url)
    - builds a table of extracted rows
    - sends the generated HTML to the background script for copying
    - updates the status banner with completion info

- chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(function(request, sender, sendResponse) {...})
  - Purpose: listens for the popup's extract command.
  - How it is used: receives the message, immediately responds, and starts run().

4) linkedin_profile.js
- generateTable(html_to_insert)
  - Purpose: same as the list version; creates the final HTML table.

- generateTableEntry(first, last, role, location, link)
  - Purpose: creates the table row for one profile.

- generateBanner()
  - Purpose: shows scraping status on the current profile page.

- lockedProfile()
  - Purpose: checks whether the current LinkedIn profile page is locked.
  - How it is used: called by getProfile().

- unlock()
  - Purpose: clicks the unlock button when the profile is locked.
  - How it is used: used by getProfile() before reading profile details.

- titleCase(str)
  - Purpose: formats text into title case.

- formatName(name)
  - Purpose: splits and formats the display name into first and last name.

- getDetails()
  - Purpose: extracts the current profile's first name, last name, job title, location, and public profile URL directly from the page.
  - How it is used: called after the profile has been unlocked.

- getProfile()
  - Purpose: runs the unlock-and-extract workflow for a single profile page.
  - How it is used: called by run().
  - Behavior: rejects if unlock fails, otherwise resolves with the extracted details.

- run()
  - Purpose: main execution function for the single-profile mode.
  - How it is used: called when the content script receives the extract command.
  - Workflow:
    - extracts one profile
    - builds a table row
    - sends the HTML to the background script
    - shows success or unlock-needed status

- chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(function(request, sender, sendResponse) {...})
  - Purpose: listens for the popup's extract command and starts scraping.

How the extension works end to end
1. The popup button is clicked.
2. popup.js sends an extract command to the active tab.
3. The correct content script runs based on the current LinkedIn page.
4. The content script scrapes profile data.
5. The data is converted into an HTML table.
6. The content script sends that HTML to background.js.
7. background.js copies the HTML to the clipboard.

Important notes
- The extension depends on jQuery.
- It targets LinkedIn Recruiter pages only.
- It works by injecting hidden iframes and reading DOM content from LinkedIn pages.
- Some parts are fragile because they depend on LinkedIn's page structure and button text.
